    <sys:String x:Key="Acc.Help">Keys: up and down arrows read slides without changing what the congregation sees. Page Down and Page Up move the projected image. Control with Page Down and Page Up moves to the next and previous song of the setlist. Enter projects the slide you are reading. B blanks and restores the screen. S tells what the congregation sees. R repeats the slide being read. F2 checks the screens. Control with F or F3 opens song search: type a number or title, press Enter, pick a song with the arrows, Enter adds it to the end of the setlist, Control with Enter adds and projects it at once, Escape closes the search. L reads the whole setlist, telling which song is on screen and where you are standing. Alt with the up and down arrows moves the setlist cursor without changing anything for the congregation; Alt with Home and End jumps to the first and last song of the setlist; Alt with Enter projects the song under the cursor. Delete removes the song under the cursor from the setlist: the first Delete asks, the second removes, Escape cancels. Control with Shift and Page Up or Page Down moves the song under the cursor one place in the setlist. Control with S saves the setlist: type a name and press Enter. Control with O opens a saved setlist: type a part of the name, press the down arrow to reach the list, pick a setlist and press Enter; Delete on the list removes a saved setlist from the database, also with two presses. F1 is this help.</sys:String>
